This was my fifth ascension; first lawful, and first as a monk. I
decided to forego the monk-related conducts early (weaponless,
vegetarian), and used Excalibur through most of the game. I ate corpses
to gain a few necessary intrinsics (telepathy, disintegration
resistance).

An altar at Level 4 served as my base throughout the game. Once a brown
pudding was generated there, I set up a nice little "pudding zoo" using
Elbereth and one side of the altar room, and kept a set of puddings
there for the rest of the game. Whenever I wanted to do some farming,
I'd hit a few of those until the divided ones were created on the
Elbereth squares, then move to the altar to get the proper conveyor
belt going. This was my first time farming, and I was able to get some
good armor, a couple of magic markers, and a few dozen spellbooks out
of it.

I spent an early wish on an amulet of reflection after determining that
Sokoban didn't have one. Later I used a shield for reflection (removing
it to cast spells), and used the amulet slot for life saving (never
used). The cloak of magic resistance came from a wizard's bones pile,
the boots and gauntlets were found, and the helmet and T-shirt were
wishes.

I managed to get my AC down to -41, which was a challenge without body
armor. A +3 ring of protection is what finally pushed me over the -40
limit. It would have been better, but I accidentally sacrificed a
werewolf and lost 15 points of protection (later regaining 11).

There were no major challenges in this game, other than ordinary stuff.
I had powerful pets thanks to a poly trap, and had pretty much reached
"walking tank" status before entering either the Castle or the Quest,
so even Master Kaen went down easily in melee.

I used magic mapping liberally in Gehennom, and the major demons
weren't a problem. I even managed to get Orcus' wand fully charged when
I fell down a deep trap door and came up right next to him (with a
cockatrice egg handy). I think I found a total of seven wands of death
in this game.

Finding the vibrating square was a little more trouble than usual; I
had to walk through almost the entire level before finding it. The
Sanctum was easy with conflict, and even the mysterious force didn't
hassle me too much (maybe 10 extra level crossings).

The planes were a breeze. On Astral, since things were going so well I
decided to have a little fun. Thanks to a lot of boulders from a lot of
giants, I jailed Death in the leftmost temple while I cleared out that
wing of the level, then kept Famine and Pestilence at bay while
clearing out everything else. I jailed Famine and Pestilence
side-by-side next to the lawful temple on the right, and emptied,
recharged, and re-emptied all my wands of death into them, until I was
out of magic markers and blank scrolls. Then I let Death chase me
around and killed it a few dozen times in melee, before finally letting
Pesty and Famine out of their jail for a free-for-all. Finally I got
bored with the whole thing and ascended.





